  "scope": "An actual fixed 84-instruction program traverses each original stored Boolean adjacency row, reads its row-retention flag, calls the real conjunction row program with the same full column-retention mask, and preserves actual returned row roots in order. The same physical run includes final halt with an input-only linear matrix-cell-count bound. Both directions of the old adjacency storage representation and exact original keptAdjacency output equality are proved. Represented retention flags and row/column alignment remain inputs; joining the actual original-cost-row retained-mask constructor is separate.",
